  "live_records": {
    "q-344305": {
      "dom_id": "step-q344305",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6},$ calculate $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}.$\n\n| $\\text{d}y$ | $=$ | $8{x}^{5}$ |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| $\\text{d}x$ |  | {{field-1}} |",
      "worked_solution": "$$\n\nThe formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡4{x}^{6}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{(4{x}^{6})}^{2}+1}}\\cdot {(4{x}^{6})}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}\\cdot 24{x}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{8{x}^{5}}{\\sqrt{16{x}^{12}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "field-1",
