    "q-95242": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95242",
      "name": "Question 2",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x,$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic sine function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{{x}^{2}+1}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(3\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{arsinh}⁡2x) \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{(2x)^{2}+1}}\\cdot (2x)^{′} \\\\  & =3\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}\\cdot 2 \\\\  & =\\frac{6}{\\sqrt{4{x}^{2}+1}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
