    "q-96442": {
      "dom_id": "step-q96442",
      "name": "Question 5",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(3x-1)) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(3x-1)}^{2}}\\cdot {(3x-1)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-(9{x}^{2}-6x+1)}\\cdot 3 \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{3}\\cdot \\frac{1}{6x-9{x}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3x(2-3x)}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
