    "q-95515": {
      "dom_id": "step-q95515",
      "name": "Question 6",
      "problem": "$$\n\nIf $y=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x),$ then $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=$",
      "worked_solution": "The formula for the derivative of the inverse hyperbolic tangent function is\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x)=\\frac{1}{1-{x}^{2}}.\n$$\n\nUsing the formula above with the chain rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)) \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-{(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{2}}\\cdot {(\\sqrt{6}\\,x)}^{′} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{2}\\cdot \\frac{1}{1-6{x}^{2}}\\cdot \\sqrt{6} \\\\  & =\\frac{2\\sqrt{3}}{1-6{x}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-95515-a",
              "type": "math",
              "value": "\\frac{\\sqrt{3}}{6{x}^{2}-1}",
